Rhoform third-party notices
===========================

This file reproduces the licence text of third-party work that Rhoform
credits. Each entry records the licence basis for carrying it, what (if
anything) was copied, and where the reproduced text came from -- the source URL
at a pinned commit, the git blob id and a SHA-256 -- which is the record
AGENTS.md asks for before the repository redistributes third-party material.
The project's own licensing is described in LICENSES.md and NOTICE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
atopile
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Why this notice is here

    Requirement L2 reads: "Adopt atopile's MIT-licensed surface with public
    attribution." Rhoform adopts constructs of atopile's surface syntax --
    principally the `module` and `new` keywords and the `~` connection
    operator -- and owes atopile public attribution for them. The attribution
    itself is the "Attribution" section of LICENSES.md; this entry carries the
    licence text that section refers to.

What is and is not copied

    No atopile code, grammar text or documentation is copied into this
    repository. Rhoform's grammar is generated from an original rule table
    (lang/grammar/rhoform_syntax.py), and the bake-off candidate that stayed
    closest to atopile's surface is the one that lost. The only atopile-related
    text in the tree is four short quotations from public atopile issue and
    pull-request discussions in corpus/bugs.yaml (BUG-0038 to BUG-0041). They
    are their individual authors' prose, not material under the licence below,
    and they are covered by the corpus/bugs.yaml entry in NOTICE.

